#
# Citation metadata (CFF 1.2.0): renders GitHub's "Cite this repository"
# button (APA and BibTeX). Kept release-accurate: every release cut sets
# `version` and `date-released` with scripts/release/version.sh, which also
# updates .zenodo.json. The `citation` CI job (scripts/checks/citation.sh)
# validates this file against the vendored schema in .github/cff-schema/,
# holds `version` to package.json, and holds .zenodo.json to this file.
# `date-released` is absent until the first release; the cut adds it.
# `identifiers` (the Zenodo concept DOI) is added once the first release is
# archived (docs/release.md, "Citation and Zenodo").
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "eduLIMS"
abstract: >-
  An open-source laboratory information management system (LIMS) for
  practical laboratory education. Students register samples, upload and check
  measurements and submit lab reports; teachers grade with a rubric and follow
  a KPI dashboard. Measurement data is stored as openEHR compositions in
  FerroEHR.
authors:
  - family-names: Talstra
    given-names: Ruben
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-2758-0141"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vernum-Projecten/eduLIMS"
url: "https://edulims.eu"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - LIMS
  - laboratory information management system
  - laboratory education
  - practical education
  - sample management
  - openEHR
  - HL7 v2
  - TypeScript
  - TanStack Start
  - PostgreSQL
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
